   The production-safety claim is false. `isPrivateIPv6` only recognizes dotted IPv4-mapped forms, while the URL parser canonicalizes them to hexadecimal. A direct runtime check showed both `https://[::ffff:127.0.0.1]` and `https://[::ffff:10.0.0.1]` are accepted with `allowHttp:false, allowLocal:false`. DNS names resolving to private addresses are also never resolved before validation. The new UI therefore promises SSRF protection the implementation does not provide.

